{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Importing at call sites","type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Comparison","type":"heading","anchor":"Comparison","level":3},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"None","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":" only","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Construction only","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Target"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading"},{"name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Registration-Order","type":"heading","text":"Registration Order"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"anchor":"Explanation"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","title":"PluginHost","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","title":"Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"title":"Undo \/ Redo","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"type":"topic","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"type":"topic","title":"Store","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Design Principles","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","title":"EntityStore","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]}}}